== LangMem-inspired agent memory ==
An agent forms memories on the hot path and in a debounced background queue, keeps a single profile document current, and revises its own prompt from feedback.
Genie structures: ownership tree, keyed collection, two versioned records, event log, temporal collection, lineage DAG

Tools available to the agent:
- manage_memory: Write one memory now, under memories/dana. Permitted: create | update.
- search_memory: Search memories below memories/dana by text and metadata.
- submit_conversation: Queue a conversation for background memory formation, debounced per thread.
- run_reflection: Apply every submission that has come due. Manager permissions: insert=true, update=true, delete=true.
- get_profile: Read the single 'preferences' document and the versions before it.
- optimize_prompt: Fold feedback on past exchanges into a prompt, if it changes the rules.
- get_prompt: Read the prompt the agent runs with, its rules, and its earlier versions.

Agent answer:
Question: Should I approve the Litestar diff for Dana?
Procedural memory (code-review r2, from review-812-feedback):
  Review the diff and report what will break.
  Rules learned from feedback:
  1. Name the test that fails in every comment.
  2. Lead with what breaks before any style comment.
